# Load GPU driver
# registerMemBase/irqLine are required: the gpu@e0f00000 DT node is
# status="disabled" and gpu_driver has no of_match_table, so galcore only
# ever binds through the legacy drv_init() module-param path -- without
# these, it silently defaults to registerMemBase=0x80000000 (wrong physical
# address for this SoC's GPU registers, real one is 0xe0f00000) and
# irqLine=-1.
#
# contiguousSize=0x800000 (2026-07-22, corrected from an earlier 0x400000
# "fix"): that earlier value came from a commented-out reference line in
# stock's etc/all.sh/etc/rc.d/rcS, never actually executed on real
# hardware. Stock's REAL, active, unconditionally-executed insmod line
# (etc/profile, sourced on every login -- the same mechanism this project
# already established launches MsnCoreApp itself, not rcS) uses
# contiguousSize=0x800000. Restored to match. This is galcore's own GPU
# memory pool size -- see docs/DEVICE_TEST_CHECKLIST_2026-07-18.md
# section 21/22 for why this pool is directly implicated in the ongoing
# red/black-screen investigation (surfaces allocated from it may never
# reach the actual displayed framebuffer) -- a too-small pool is a real,
# independent discrepancy from stock worth fixing regardless of whether
# it's also part of that root cause.
modprobe galcore registerMemBase=0xE0F00000 irqLine=32 contiguousSize=0x800000 physSize=0x80000000 powerManagement=0

# Load USB WiFi driver
# rtw_drv_log_level=2 (_DRV_ERR_, lowered from 3/_DRV_WARNING_ 2026-07-31 --
# WARNING level in this vendor driver is still routinely noisy, not
# reserved for genuinely exceptional conditions) keeps real errors visible
# while dropping routine driver-internal chatter. Default is _DRV_INFO_=4.
# See include/rtw_debug.h in the driver source.
# rtw_country_code=US added 2026-08-04: without a valid HW (EFUSE) or SW
# channel plan, this driver's rtw_rfctl_decide_init_chplan() (new in the
# 2025-03-27 SDK update -- the old driver had no channel-plan/regulatory
# validation at all) falls back to RTW_CHPLAN_WORLDWIDE (chplan 0x7F),
# which excludes 5GHz UNII-1 channels (36/40/44/48). This is the module's
# very first load at boot -- well before wifi_ap.sh or MsnCoreApp ever
# run -- so without this, every later reload inherits/re-derives the same
# restrictive default unless something else supplies a country code.
# Hardware-confirmed: this fix (paired with the matching insmod in
# etc/hostapd.sh, MsnCoreApp's own reload path) resolves the "wireless
# CarPlay/Android Auto never connects" symptom -- hostapd was rejecting
# the dynamic hw_mode=a channel=36 AP config with "Configured channel
# (36) not found from the channel list of current mode... Could not
# select hw_mode and channel. (-3)" until a real channel plan (0x1B, US)
# was available. See docs/VENDOR_BSP_RESEARCH.md and
# project_wireless_carplay_aa_channel_plan memory for the full trace.
modprobe rtl8811cu rtw_drv_log_level=2 rtw_country_code=US

# Set up DHCP lease directory and file
mkdir -p /data
touch /data/udhcpd.leases

# Disabled 2026-07-24: this static-SSID AP (etc/wifi_ap.sh, added by this
# reconstruction project -- confirmed absent from the real stock rootfs
# dump) was previously believed to match stock's real boot behavior, but
# that was never actually verified against a live wireless Android
# Auto/CarPlay connection. It does the opposite: `sink` (usr/bin/sink)
# dynamically generates a per-connection SSID (e.g. "carplay_fc9f") and
# tells the phone to join THAT network over Bluetooth (confirmed via
# decompile + a live connection log, docs/DEVICE_TEST_CHECKLIST_2026-07-18.md).
# With this static "carplay_wifi" AP already bound to wlan0 from boot,
# sink's own attempt to (re)configure hostapd to match never takes
# effect, the phone can't find/join the SSID it was told, and it reports
# connect_status=0 (failure) back over Bluetooth -- exactly the "connects
# via Bluetooth, video never loads" symptom. Leaving wlan0 free for
# sink's own dynamic AP setup instead. STA mode is still available by
# hand if needed for SSH/testing: uncomment/run etc/wifi_client.sh (see
# docs/DRIVER_TEST_PLAN.md and the comment at the top of each script).
#/etc/wifi_ap.sh &
#/etc/wifi_client.sh &

# 2026-08-03: auto-start MsnCoreApp (the main UI) at boot -- now that
# U-Boot's own reliability work (cold-boot hangs, noise-triggered
# autoboot aborts) has settled down, moving from fully-manual startup
# toward normal unattended operation. Deliberately NOT resurrecting
# stock's own mechanism for this: stock's /etc/profile unconditionally
# ran MsnFirstInit + `MsnCoreApp -qws&` on every login shell, which
# this project intentionally disabled 2026-07-14 (see that file's own
# comment) because /etc/profile is sourced on *every* SSH/serial/telnet
# session, not just once at boot -- it was silently respawning a second
# compositor instance and fighting live framebuffer/driver tests
# (tools/lcd-test, tools/ark1680-ts-test, etc.) that expect the real
# one to stay down while testing. rcS runs exactly once, at real boot,
# so it doesn't have that problem -- this is the right place for an
# actual "start on boot" behavior, distinct from stock's login-shell
# hack. start_msn_directfb (not start_msn_linuxfb) is the
# GPU-accelerated DirectFB backend -- matched-pair galcore.ko/libGAL.so
# and the galcore modprobe above are both already in place by this
# point in the script. Backgrounded (&) so rcS itself still returns and
# the console/diagnostic banner below remain usable.
#
# 2026-08-03: real hardware testing found launching it immediately
# here raced with something not fully ready yet -- a kernel-level
# page fault landed mid-init, right in the galcore/Vivante GPU driver
# path. A 5s delay alone (below) did NOT fix it, same crash -- ruling
# out pure settle-time and pointing at a real environment difference
# instead: rcS never sources /etc/profile, but every SSH/serial login
# shell does (it's a login shell), so a manual run always has
# /etc/profile's exports in place first, then start_msn_directfb's own
# on top -- CARPLAY_*/PROTOCOL_ID/TOUCHSERIAL and, notably,
# /tmp/touch_export (QWS_MOUSE_PROTO/QWS_ARK_MT_DEVICE -- see
# project_touch_qws_env_gate -- created by the touchdriver block
# earlier in this same script, but only ever sourced by /etc/profile,
# never by start_msn_directfb itself) are all silently missing when
# launched straight from rcS. Sourcing /etc/profile first in the same
# subshell closes that gap; start_msn_directfb's own exports on top
# still take effect exactly as they do interactively.
#
# HARDWARE-CONFIRMED WORKING 2026-08-03: sourcing /etc/profile was the
# real fix -- the missing environment, not settle time. Delay dropped
# from 5s to 1s and retested clean, confirming the 5s value was never
# doing the real work; 1s is kept only as a trivial safety margin for
# /etc/profile's own dependencies (e.g. /tmp/touch_export) rather than
# anything galcore/GPU-related.
(sleep 1 && . /etc/profile && /usr/bin/start_msn_directfb) &

# --- diagnostic tools banner (firmware_overlay/prado) ---
